[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186204581 :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$42$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ {y}_{2} & {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1+2+3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 42 & 24 & 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203420 :answer-field/correct "answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer/id #uuid "dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203419 :answer-field/correct "answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer-field/choices ["answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer/id #uuid "316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203422 :answer-field/correct "answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer/id #uuid "d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203421 :answer-field/correct "answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer/id #uuid "f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204589 :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} & {y}_{1} \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({0}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\ 0+2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203456 :answer-field/correct "answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer/id #uuid "6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203454 :answer-field/correct "answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer/id #uuid "ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203455 :answer-field/correct "answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer/id #uuid "a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204100 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" "question-8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/id #uuid "9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/math-academy-id "q-269802" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{3},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,-1,\\,3]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -7 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" "answer-field-b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" "answer-field-ff075b7b-7ca8-5b8f-88a3-0b6d0e198ed4" "answer-field-0d008ce6-0db4-5560-8335-4e57b2ea4c0d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/id #uuid "91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer/id #uuid "eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer/id #uuid "d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ff075b7b-7ca8-5b8f-88a3-0b6d0e198ed4" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff075b7b-7ca8-5b8f-88a3-0b6d0e198ed4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e" :answer/id #uuid "15b1b88d-fa4a-5ce4-858f-cbf3ca4ba87e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0d008ce6-0db4-5560-8335-4e57b2ea4c0d" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d008ce6-0db4-5560-8335-4e57b2ea4c0d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7" :answer/id #uuid "d9e31081-73fb-57ae-a678-67ffc4cb37a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a" :question/id #uuid "8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-269803" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{3},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[2,\\,-1,\\,1]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-726def4a-0906-5fa9-9043-394665a07fc7" "answer-field-fe571652-a4d2-5aca-a284-5cc14e649fc0" "answer-field-bd92e62f-367e-5106-b7b7-0a4661d602b0" "answer-field-183c83b2-fe77-525b-a49f-d3a9ba2e786a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-726def4a-0906-5fa9-9043-394665a07fc7" :answer-field/id #uuid "726def4a-0906-5fa9-9043-394665a07fc7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-72e6ae6d-bb8d-5cc2-a28a-14459e3d01bb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72e6ae6d-bb8d-5cc2-a28a-14459e3d01bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72e6ae6d-bb8d-5cc2-a28a-14459e3d01bb" :answer/id #uuid "72e6ae6d-bb8d-5cc2-a28a-14459e3d01bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe571652-a4d2-5aca-a284-5cc14e649fc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe571652-a4d2-5aca-a284-5cc14e649fc0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0e09df5c-3585-5850-8211-9855817d7292" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e09df5c-3585-5850-8211-9855817d7292"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e09df5c-3585-5850-8211-9855817d7292" :answer/id #uuid "0e09df5c-3585-5850-8211-9855817d7292" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd92e62f-367e-5106-b7b7-0a4661d602b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd92e62f-367e-5106-b7b7-0a4661d602b0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3f6bd7f7-3c1a-5787-a2e8-9c30e81f2652" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3f6bd7f7-3c1a-5787-a2e8-9c30e81f2652"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f6bd7f7-3c1a-5787-a2e8-9c30e81f2652" :answer/id #uuid "3f6bd7f7-3c1a-5787-a2e8-9c30e81f2652" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-183c83b2-fe77-525b-a49f-d3a9ba2e786a" :answer-field/id #uuid "183c83b2-fe77-525b-a49f-d3a9ba2e786a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-09b99397-4784-52a1-bc2e-c34d594af14b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09b99397-4784-52a1-bc2e-c34d594af14b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09b99397-4784-52a1-bc2e-c34d594af14b" :answer/id #uuid "09b99397-4784-52a1-bc2e-c34d594af14b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204101 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760" :question/id #uuid "ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760" :question/math-academy-id "q-269823" :question/problem "For $x,y,z\\in {R}^{2},$ consider the following functions: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & y(x)=Ax\\,\\text{where}\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & z(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & f(z)=Cz\\,\\text{where}\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x)))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $z\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $C$ and outputs a vector $f(z)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}=C.\n$$\n\n- The function $z$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $z(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{z}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1} & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=A{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2(-1) & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(z(y(x))){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}z}{|}_{{z}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34d7e51d-85f2-564b-a3f7-2300578f216d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34d7e51d-85f2-564b-a3f7-2300578f216d" :answer-field/id #uuid "34d7e51d-85f2-564b-a3f7-2300578f216d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e1a2103-5199-5776-8be3-a4b90b89af36" "answer-80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" "answer-22bf0f43-71c0-5fe6-8a9c-db88987e135d" "answer-88597b94-66f0-5510-9176-e7d043bbb584" "answer-b3d925c6-ea55-56ff-b092-6a1d99103f84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e1a2103-5199-5776-8be3-a4b90b89af36" :answer/id #uuid "7e1a2103-5199-5776-8be3-a4b90b89af36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" :answer/id #uuid "80264191-38a9-5a0e-9ad8-7978f8daa096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22bf0f43-71c0-5fe6-8a9c-db88987e135d" :answer/id #uuid "22bf0f43-71c0-5fe6-8a9c-db88987e135d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88597b94-66f0-5510-9176-e7d043bbb584" :answer/id #uuid "88597b94-66f0-5510-9176-e7d043bbb584" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3d925c6-ea55-56ff-b092-6a1d99103f84" :answer/id #uuid "b3d925c6-ea55-56ff-b092-6a1d99103f84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e93dbd98-aef9-5df9-aea8-c85d4eb5eb85" :activity/id #uuid "e93dbd98-aef9-5df9-aea8-c85d4eb5eb85" :activity/title "The Chain Rule for Total Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048367 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" "step-b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" "step-01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" "step-99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" "step-6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0"] :activity/first-step "step-aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" :step/id #uuid "aeffc49e-02fd-5851-a96c-59f1d28fc3f8" :step/content 17592186204581 :step/next "step-b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" :step/id #uuid "b0e4ff39-21d5-5469-8555-eb4203698626" :step/content 17592186204589 :step/next "step-01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" :step/id #uuid "01c39290-cd5a-5aa1-8a59-9cbfefffe951" :step/content "question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :step/next "step-99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" :step/id #uuid "99a98175-6d17-5897-8ff6-309efa769d68" :step/content "question-8583a74c-8e9b-50f5-aea2-c01f0aa03b2a" :step/next "step-6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0" :step/id #uuid "6ceaa452-9af3-59b8-a7ac-18a86e3a74a0" :step/content "question-ed9f515f-42d2-575d-bafa-bcd19e12a760" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186204581 :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$42$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [17592186204581 :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ {y}_{2} & {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1+2+3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 42 & 24 & 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186204581 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer/id #uuid "dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e"] ["answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e" :answer/value "7"] [17592186203420 :answer-field/correct "answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e"] [17592186203420 :answer-field/choices "answer-dcc67051-2347-5c4e-9e43-c494abdd7e5e"] ["answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer/id #uuid "316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33"] ["answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33" :answer/value "4"] [17592186203419 :answer-field/correct "answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33"] [17592186203419 :answer-field/choices "answer-316633d4-c832-597f-bfdd-ba8fe21eae33"] ["answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer/id #uuid "d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb"] ["answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb" :answer/value "3"] [17592186203422 :answer-field/correct "answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb"] [17592186203422 :answer-field/choices "answer-d6616688-0122-57c7-8244-6a4ed78090eb"] ["answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer/id #uuid "f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be"] ["answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be" :answer/value "24"] [17592186203421 :answer-field/correct "answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be"] [17592186203421 :answer-field/choices "answer-f5702173-007e-5e88-ab6b-3cfa857c23be"] [17592186204589 :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [17592186204589 :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} & {y}_{1} \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({0}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\ 0+2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186204589 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer/id #uuid "6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722"] ["answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722" :answer/value "2"] [17592186203456 :answer-field/correct "answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722"] [17592186203456 :answer-field/choices "answer-6f15b05f-36f5-5ea3-9bed-f930f886c722"] ["answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer/id #uuid "ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c"] ["answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c" :answer/value "6"] [17592186203454 :answer-field/correct "answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c"] [17592186203454 :answer-field/choices "answer-ec5a3336-3253-558e-8eea-a50f43e5289c"] ["answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer/id #uuid "a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e"] ["answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e" :answer/value "12"] [17592186203455 :answer-field/correct "answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e"] [17592186203455 :answer-field/choices "answer-a6a5ce82-7ccb-54b4-abfb-a30641f2c77e"] ["question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/id #uuid "9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40"] ["question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/math-academy-id "q-269802"] ["question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{3},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,-1,\\,3]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -7 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9684ce08-aa53-5b58-9612-0d1c154cab40" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/id #uuid "91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24"] ["answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer/id #uuid "eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb"] ["answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/correct "answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb"] ["answer-field-91938b79-0782-57b7-a58c-c38b652b5f24" :answer-field/choices "answer-eb2b7682-cd57-5046-9330-476f79bd0afb"] ["answer-field-b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46"] ["answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer/id #uuid "d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188"] ["answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d12784d6-1d33-593b-ad17-021cbcd94188" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-field-b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-b6a101ae-6c02-52e5-9871-130a767d9a46" :answer-field/type :an